Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Take the system DPI from WINEDROID_DPI on Android.

The DPI of the Android screen reached Wine through the driver's
config_changed event, which stores it in the registry. The desktop
process has read the system DPI by then, and gives it to the display
source, so the monitor DPI (used by per-monitor aware programs such as
Chromium and VS Code) stayed at the previous session's value.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index eee8149..863b4c4 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -5889,6 +5900,15 @@ void sysparams_init(void)
             NtClose( hkey );
         }
     }
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+    /* WineDroid passes the DPI of the Android screen: its desktop process starts
+     * before the driver can store it in the registry, and gave the monitor the
+     * DPI of the previous session */
+    {
+        const char *env = getenv( "WINEDROID_DPI" );
+        if (env && atoi( env ) > 0) system_dpi = atoi( env );
+    }
+#endif
     if (!system_dpi) system_dpi = USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI;
 
     /* FIXME: what do the DpiScalingVer flags mean? */
